                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec467145-194f-3f26-89d3-e0657bf1f3a2",
                        "entry_id": "a3b7df42-7a43-3fca-ac0d-4fe07151dce6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To sing inadequately, or with too little vocal effort."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c889f62-f81d-4bb9-8ab4-ac94a85caa48",
                                "sense_id": "ec467145-194f-3f26-89d3-e0657bf1f3a2",
                                "text": "…the enthusiastic borderism of Scott, who, rather than that a freebooter should under-act his part, or a bard undersing his praise, took the liberty of sometimes inventing the action and then resounding its glories, and debiting both to the account of originals, quite innocent of either."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d46a787-a696-4981-b49b-50eb410172f8",
                                "sense_id": "ec467145-194f-3f26-89d3-e0657bf1f3a2",
                                "text": "But the night’s true indictment of country’s man problem was the dullness of the performances by male stars exponentially more famous than Mr. Stapleton: Zac Brown, undersinging on “Beautiful Drug”; Kenny Chesney’s lethargic turn on “Save It for a Rainy Day”; Blake Shelton mugging for the cameras on “Gonna,” Dierks Bentley needlessly stoic on “Riser.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fd1d670-d0a6-30de-a424-34cc92ab418d",
                        "entry_id": "a3b7df42-7a43-3fca-ac0d-4fe07151dce6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To sing beneath, or in accompaniment to; to sing an undersong."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "83aac0a5-02bb-4d60-b6b6-326cabf09640",
                                "sense_id": "0fd1d670-d0a6-30de-a424-34cc92ab418d",
                                "text": "Alas me! what a murmur and motion I hear,\nAs of birds flying near!\nAnd the air undersings\nThe soft stroke of their wings—\nAnd all life that approaches, I wait for in fear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60613d8e-81db-4575-ad85-5dec36119c12",
                                "sense_id": "0fd1d670-d0a6-30de-a424-34cc92ab418d",
                                "text": "Other post-Spenserian undersongs resonate with some of these implications… But even here, the stream of time is clearly the source of the Spenserian undersinging."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
